<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Neum</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Neum is a small town on the Adriatic coast that forms <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/herzegovina">Herzegovina</a>'s only access to the sea, a strip about 9 kilometres wide dividing Croatian territory. Under the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/treaty-of-karlowitz">Treaty of Karlowitz</a> of 1699 the Republic of Ragusa secured Ottoman possession of the strip as a buffer separating it from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/venetian-dalmatia">Venetian Dalmatia</a>. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peljesac">Pelješac</a> Bridge, opened in 2022, links Croatian territory across it.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/neum.jpg" alt="Neum" width="320" height="160" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author this version: Željko Heimer · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Neum,_Bosnia_and_Herzegovina.gif" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
